# Layouts and Responsive Design

Single source of truth for breakpoints, shell behavior, and content width.

## Breakpoints

| Token | Width | Layout |
|---|---|---|
| `xs`/`sm` | `< 600` | mobile, one column |
| `md` | `600–839` | large mobile / small tablet |
| `lg` | `840–1199` | tablet / small desktop, rail |
| `xl` | `1200–1599` | desktop: menu bar, side nav |
| `xxl` | `≥ 1600` | large desktop, max-width |

## Requirements

- Use centralized responsive utilities in `lib/core/responsive/`.
- Must not duplicate screens per size unless the interaction model changes.
- Scale one-column to multi-column; use readable max widths and must not use fixed widths.
- Keep touch and pointer targets comfortable per platform.
- Keep shell and content-width behavior uniform across modules.
- Reusable layout components must live in `frontend/lib/shared/layout/`.
- Localize navigation text; omit destinations for unauthorized users (RBAC+ABAC, [`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; use design tokens only ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).

## Navigation by width

- `< 600`: app bar plus bottom navigation or drawer.
- `600–1199`: navigation rail or compact side navigation.
- `≥ 1200`: menu bar and side navigation (collapsed `64–80`, expanded `220–280`); persist collapsed state as a non-sensitive preference.

## Max content widths

- Auth forms `420–520`; general forms `560–720`; detail pages `840–1040`; dashboards `1200–1440`; data-heavy `1440`+.

